                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>In the evening of May 5, Eden and Molotov met for dinner, during the course of
                    which substantive discussions on Korea and Indochina took place. Eden gave an account of the meeting to Smith, who reported to the Department in
                    telegram Secto 115, May 6, not printed. The
                    telegram contained the following brief passage on Korea: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Eden said he was not optimistic
                            over prospects of any settlement on Korea unless Russians could prevail
                            upon Chinese and North Koreans to abandon their wholly unreasonable
                            attitude. He did not envisage this happening but thought continuation of
                                <hi rendition="#italic">status quo</hi> in Korea not too bad.
                                Molotov indicated agreement.”
                            (396.1 GE/5–654)</p></quote></p>
            </div>
